---
import WikiLayout from '../layouts/WikiLayout.astro';
import { repoUrl } from '../lib/wiki.js';
---

<WikiLayout title="Contributors" description="The people behind Kenshi Wiki, the origins of Outland, and terms for reusing wiki material." source="src/pages/contributors.astro">
  <div class="credits">
    <p><a href="https://github.com/VlcekM">VlcekM</a> built the original Astro prototype and proposed RimWorld Wiki as the model for its presentation. Prd (<a href="https://github.com/mattresspad">mattresspad</a>) founded and maintains Kenshi Wiki, added the ecosystem navigation, and set up the site’s Cloudflare deployment. The wiki’s theme, Outland, adapts the legacy Vector skin and styling from RimWorld Wiki.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/teppuM">teppuM</a> documented how Skeleton Repair Beds heal damage and when skeletons repair themselves. Their <a href={`${repoUrl}/pull/8`}>article edits</a> include links to saves and test notes other players can check.</p>
    <p>Have a correction of your own? <a href={`${repoUrl}/issues/new?template=article-correction.yml`}>Tell us which article and what to change</a>, or use <strong>Edit on GitHub</strong> on that article to propose the wording yourself.</p>
    <p>The <a href={`${repoUrl}/commits/main/`}>repository history</a> records individual changes.</p>

    <h2 id="licensing">Licenses and reuse</h2>
    <p>Original wiki article text is available under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International</a>. Credit the article and its contributors, link the license, and indicate your changes. Adaptations of that text must also meet the share-alike terms. <a href="/notices/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt">Full license text</a>.</p>
    <p>Many articles are adapted from the <a href="https://kenshi.fandom.com/">Kenshi Fandom wiki</a> and remain under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported</a>. Each says so at its foot and links the Fandom revision it came from and that page’s history, which lists its authors. Their images were not imported. <a href="/notices/CC-BY-SA-3.0.txt">Full license text</a>.</p>
    <p>The project has deferred choosing a general license for its original software. Imported code, artwork, and trademarks have their own terms.</p>

    <h2 id="outland">Outland sources</h2>
    <p>Trevor Parscal, Roan Kattouw, and the other <a href="https://github.com/wikimedia/mediawiki-skins-Vector/tree/1e084256a129ca0e57a356c263808f98f3fdf3a4">Vector contributors</a> created the legacy skin. Outland adapts its navigation and styles for Astro, with a Kenshi palette, theme switching, and a sticky ribbon. <a href="/notices/MediaWiki-CREDITS.txt">MediaWiki contributors</a> supplied the article styles and skinning graphics. The upstream projects specify GPL-2.0-or-later and identify exceptions in their notices.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Editable styles used by this build: <a href="/sources/outland.css.txt">base and article CSS</a> and <a href="/sources/wiki-header.css.txt">ribbon CSS</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/notices/upstream-skin-source.zip">Download the historical Vector and MediaWiki sources</a>, including LESS, graphics, and a file-by-file source index.</li>
      <li><a href="/notices/Vector-COPYING.txt">Vector license</a> and <a href="/notices/MediaWiki-COPYING.txt">MediaWiki notices and license</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="https://rimworldwiki.com/index.php?title=MediaWiki:Common.css&amp;action=history">RimWorld Wiki stylesheet contributors</a> and <a href="https://rimworldwiki.com/index.php?title=Main_Page&amp;action=history">main-page contributors</a> provided the <a href="https://rimworldwiki.com/index.php?oldid=180015">site CSS</a> and <a href="https://rimworldwiki.com/index.php?oldid=183085">main-page arrangement</a> adapted for Kenshi. Local changes include the category links, theme colors, and infobox headings. The wiki publishes a <a href="https://rimworldwiki.com/wiki/RimWorld_Wiki:Copyrights">CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported policy</a> for its own material. <a href="/notices/CC-BY-SA-3.0.txt">Full license text</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="artwork">Artwork and trademarks</h2>
    <p>Lo-Fi Games created Kenshi. The article header and six gallery images come from its <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/233860/Kenshi/">Steam store listing</a>. The ribbon uses the Meitou project’s two-moon favicon, companion-site glyphs, and the marks of the linked platforms.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/notices/artwork.txt">artwork credits and source list</a> identifies the individual files, their origins, and outstanding reuse questions. For example, the checkerboard is public domain. GitHub’s mark uses <a href="/notices/Octicons-MIT.txt">MIT-licensed Octicons artwork</a>. Trademark rights remain with the respective owners.</p>
    <p>On 7 November 2026, Outland replaced its three-pixel shadow image with a CSS gradient. The prototype used <a href="https://rimworldwiki.com/index.php?oldid=107267">game artwork uploaded to RimWorld Wiki by AcDie</a>. Earlier commits still contain that image.</p>
  </div>
</WikiLayout>

<style>
  .credits { max-width: 76ch; }
  :global(.page-Contributors #firstHeading) { display: block; }
</style>
